        <article data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext">
  
  
  <h1 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext" class="text-break">
    Interface IConsoleContext
    
  </h1>
  
  <div class="facts text-secondary">
    <dl><dt>Namespace</dt><dd><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.html">GameFramework.ConsoleTool</a></dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Assembly</dt><dd>cs.temp.dll.dll</dd></dl>
  </div>
  
  <div class="markdown summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Context interface providing access to console functionality
Allows commands to interact with the console system safely without direct access to internal state
Acts as a controlled facade that prevents commands from breaking console integrity</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">public interface IConsoleContext</code></pre>
  </div>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <h2 class="section" id="methods">Methods
  </h2>
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_EnqueueCommand_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.EnqueueCommand*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_EnqueueCommand_System_String_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.EnqueueCommand(System.String)">
    EnqueueCommand(String)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Adds a command to the execution queue without adding it to command history
Useful for batch operations, scripting, and command chaining
Commands are executed in FIFO order during the next console update</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">void EnqueueCommand(string command)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h4 class="section">Parameters</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><code>command</code> <span class="xref">System.String</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">The command string to queue (including arguments)</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_IsCommandRegistered_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.IsCommandRegistered*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_IsCommandRegistered_System_String_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.IsCommandRegistered(System.String)">
    IsCommandRegistered(String)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Checks if a command with the specified name is currently registered in the system
Useful for conditional command execution and validation in complex command scripts
Command names are case-insensitive</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">bool IsCommandRegistered(string commandName)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h4 class="section">Parameters</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><code>commandName</code> <span class="xref">System.String</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">The name of the command to check</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  <h4 class="section">Returns</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><span class="xref">System.Boolean</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">True if the command is registered and available for execution</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_SetWaitForLoad_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.SetWaitForLoad*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_SetWaitForLoad_System_Boolean_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.SetWaitForLoad(System.Boolean)">
    SetWaitForLoad(Boolean)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Sets a flag to wait for level/scene loading to complete before processing next command
Essential for commands that depend on scene state or need to execute after scene transitions
Command execution will pause until the current level finishes loading</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">void SetWaitForLoad(bool wait)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h4 class="section">Parameters</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><code>wait</code> <span class="xref">System.Boolean</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">True to wait for level load completion, false to continue normally</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_SetWaitFrames_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.SetWaitFrames*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_SetWaitFrames_System_Int32_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.SetWaitFrames(System.Int32)">
    SetWaitFrames(Int32)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Sets the number of frames to wait before processing the next queued command
Useful for timing-sensitive operations and ensuring proper frame sequencing
Command execution will pause until the specified number of frames have passed</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">void SetWaitFrames(int frames)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h4 class="section">Parameters</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><code>frames</code> <span class="xref">System.Int32</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">Number of frames to wait (must be &gt;= 0)</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_WriteError_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.WriteError*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_WriteError_System_String_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.WriteError(System.String)">
    WriteError(String)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Writes an error message to the console output with error formatting
Typically displayed in red or with error prefix to indicate failure</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">void WriteError(string message)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h4 class="section">Parameters</h4>
  <dl class="parameters">
    <dt><code>message</code> <span class="xref">System.String</span></dt>
    <dd><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="1" sourceendlinenumber="1">The error message to display</p>
</dd>
  </dl>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  <a id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_WriteLine_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.WriteLine*"></a>
  
  <h3 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_IConsoleContext_WriteLine_System_String_" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.WriteLine(System.String)">
    WriteLine(String)
    
  </h3>
  
  <div class="markdown level1 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.IConsoleContext.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Writes a standard message to the console output
Message will be displayed in the console UI and logged to Unity&apos;s console</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown level1 conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">void WriteLine(string message)</code></pre>
  </div>

